        "original_id": "6c0fe24d-6358-5cb5-8f3e-ad208e693689",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Captain James Cook\n- Artworks: Death of Cook paintings\n- Places: Kealakekua Bay, Kona coast, Hawaiʻi, Kailua-Kona\n- Topics: James Cook's 1779 death\n\nFacts:\n- In 1779, Captain James Cook died at Kealakekua Bay.\n- Death of Cook is the name of several paintings that depict the 1779 death of Captain James Cook.\n- The page describes Captain James Cook as British and as the discoverer of the Hawaiian Islands.\n- Kealakekua Bay is on the Kona coast of the island of Hawaiʻi.\n- Kealakekua Bay is about 12 miles south of Kailua-Kona.",
